 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "DualCircuitBreaker(failureThreshold, cooldown) guards a primary and a secondary server with one breaker each, both closed. A closed breaker allows attempts and counts consecutive failures; reaching failureThreshold opens it at that time and resets the count. An open breaker opened at time o allows an attempt at time t only when t - o >= cooldown; that attempt is a trial: success closes the breaker, failure reopens it at t. Any success of a closed breaker resets its count. request(timestamp, primaryOk, secondaryOk) gives the outcome each server would have: if the primary breaker allows, the primary is attempted and a success returns \"PRIMARY\"; otherwise (blocked or failed) the request is rerouted to the secondary if its breaker allows, returning \"SECONDARY\" on success and \"FAILED\" on failure; when the secondary is blocked it returns \"FAILED\" if the primary was attempted and \"BLOCKED\" if no server was attempted. Timestamps are non-decreasing. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk05-blocked-20261029-v1/contracts.json",
